    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-ayodhya-kanda-0121",
      "sequence": 498,
      "meaning": "The women helplessly yielded to the anguish of love, like cakravāka birds at evening. Knowing the hard road beneath those soft lotus feet, their crowded hearts uttered noble words: the earth shrinks from the touch of their soft, red feet just as our hearts do. If the Lord of the universe has given them the forest, why did he not make their road of flowers? If wishes could be obtained from Fate, friend, we would keep these three within our eyes. Those men and women who did not arrive in time failed to see Sītā and Rāma. Hearing of their beauty, they asked anxiously how far the brothers had gone. Whoever was able ran to behold them and returned rejoicing, having gained the fruit of birth. Women, children, and old people could only wring their hands in regret. In this way people everywhere fell under love's power wherever Rāma went.",
