    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-ayodhya-kanda-0122",
      "sequence": 499,
      "meaning": "Village after village rejoiced on seeing the moon that opens the water lilies of the solar line. Whoever learned even a little of the news blamed king and queen. Some said the king had done exceedingly well by giving their eyes this reward. The people exchanged simple, affectionate, lovely words: blessed the parents who gave them birth, blessed the city from which they came; blessed the land, mountain, forest, and village through which they passed, and blessed every place they reached. Brahmā had gained happiness by creating those who loved the travelers in every way. Along their path the delightful story of Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa spread through every road and woodland. Thus Rāma, the sun of Raghu's lotus line, gave people happiness along the way and continued onward through the forest with Sītā and Sumitrā's son.",
