    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-ayodhya-kanda-0123",
      "sequence": 500,
      "meaning": "Rāma went ahead and Lakṣmaṇa behind, both arrayed in ascetic dress and carrying its gear. Between them Sītā shone like Māyā between Brahman and the individual soul. To express the image again as it lives in the mind, she resembled Rati shining between spring and Love; or, by another inwardly chosen comparison, Rohiṇī between Mercury and the moon. Sītā carefully placed her feet between the marks of her lord's steps as she walked the road. Lakṣmaṇa kept to the right, avoiding the footprints of Sītā and Rāma. Their lovely mutual love was beyond speech; birds and beasts became absorbed in the sight, while the travelers Rāma, Lakṣmaṇa, and Sītā stole away their hearts. Every traveler who beheld the beloved brothers with Sītā reached the end of the inaccessible road of worldly existence in effortless joy.",
