      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-ayodhya-kanda-0124",
      "sequence": 501,
      "meaning": "Even now, whoever keeps the travelers Lakṣmaṇa, Sītā, and Rāma within the heart, even in a dream, will attain the path to Rāma's abode—a path that scarcely any sage ever finds. Then Raghu's hero noticed that Sītā was tired and saw nearby a cool banyan and water. They stayed there, ate roots and fruit, and at dawn bathed and continued. Viewing beautiful forests, lakes, and mountains, the lord reached Vālmīki's hermitage. Rāma saw the sage's delightful dwelling amid beautiful hills, forest, and pure water. Lotuses, trees, and woodland plants flowered by the lakes; lovely bees hummed, lost in nectar. Birds and animals made abundant sound and, free from mutual enmity, wandered with joyful minds. Seeing the pure and beautiful hermitage, the lotus-eyed prince rejoiced. Hearing of Raghu's hero's arrival, the sage came forward to receive him.",
